# Plan-anchor repository guidelines

Copy to `.sc/plan-anchor/plan-anchor-repo-guidelines.md`, keep what applies, and commit it. The repository owner maintains this file; the installer never writes it. It supplements the approved intent, the anchors and their quotes, and never overrides them (`references/anchor-document.md`). Do not put secrets or private plan text here.

## Resolving anchor conflicts

- When two anchors pull against each other, the newer locked anchor wins only if the owner said so; otherwise ask the owner.

## Triage and plan fixes

- Prefer cutting a sentence over adding one; this repository's plans are read by the people who build them.

## Question tuning

- Treat "configuration" as the committed config files only, never runtime flags.

## Drift review

- A renamed public command is material drift even when its behaviour is unchanged.

## Vocabulary

- "legacy repo": the read-only source the migration copies from.

## Known pitfalls

- Plan items that say "as before" are judged without the earlier item; restate the rule.
